{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Sir Daniel Michael Blake Day-Lewis (born 29 April 1957) is an English actor who holds both British and Irish citizenship.","title":"Daniel Day-Lewis"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Born and raised in London, he excelled on stage at the National Youth Theatre, before being accepted at the Bristol Old Vic Theatre School, which he attended for three years.","title":"Daniel Day-Lewis"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Despite his traditional actor training at the Bristol Old Vic, he is considered to be a method actor, known for his constant devotion to and research of his roles.","title":"Daniel Day-Lewis"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He would often remain completely in character for the duration of the shooting schedules of his films, even to the point of adversely affecting his health.","title":"Daniel Day-Lewis"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" He is one of the most selective actors in the film industry, having starred in only five films since 1998, with as many as five years between roles.","title":"Daniel Day-Lewis"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Protective of his private life, he rarely gives interviews and makes very few public appearances.","title":"Daniel Day-Lewis"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Nine is a 2009 romantic musical drama film directed and produced by Rob Marshall and written by Michael Tolkin and Anthony Minghella.","title":"Nine (2009 live-action film)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The film is an adaptation of the 1982 musical of the same name, which in turn is based on Federico Fellini's semi-autobiographical 1963 film "8½".","title":"Nine (2009 live-action film)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In addition to songs from the stage musical, all written by Maury Yeston, the film has three original songs, also written by Yeston.","title":"Nine (2009 live-action film)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The ensemble principal cast consists of Daniel Day-Lewis, Marion Cotillard, Penélope Cruz, Judi Dench, Fergie, Kate Hudson, Nicole Kidman, and Sophia Loren.","title":"Nine (2009 live-action film)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"British actor Christian Bale has starred in various films, as well as advertisements and a video game.","title":"Christian Bale filmography"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He made his acting debut in 1986, on the television film "".","title":"Christian Bale filmography"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The following year, he made his film debut starring alongside John Malkovich and Miranda Richardson in the war film "Empire of the Sun".","title":"Christian Bale filmography"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Bale's role of a young boy, interned in China by the Japanese, received praise from most film critics.","title":"Christian Bale filmography"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Two years later, Bale had a minor role in "Henry V", a drama film based on William Shakespeare's play "The Life of Henry the Fifth".","title":"Christian Bale filmography"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" It has been considered one of the best Shakespeare film adaptations ever made.","title":"Christian Bale filmography"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" In 1992, Bale starred as Jack Kelly in the Walt Disney musical drama "Newsies", which was a critical and commercial failure; however, it gained a cult following.","title":"Christian Bale filmography"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" He received a role in the 1994 drama "Little Women", which garnered positive reviews.","title":"Christian Bale filmography"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" Bale lent his voice for the Disney animated film "Pocahontas" in 1995, although it received a mixed reception and attained box office success.","title":"Christian Bale filmography"},{"sentence_id":9,"text":" He starred as British journalist Arthur Stuart in the Todd Haynes-directed drama "Velvet Goldmine" (1998).","title":"Christian Bale filmography"},{"sentence_id":10,"text":" Although critics were divided on the film, Bale's role was "eagerly anticipated".","title":"Christian Bale filmography"},{"sentence_id":11,"text":" Bale portrayed Demetrius in the critically praised 1999 film "A Midsummer Night's Dream", an adaptation of Shakespeare's play of the same name, directed by Michael Hoffman.","title":"Christian Bale filmography"},{"sentence_id":12,"text":" The same year, he portrayed Jesus of Nazareth in the television movie "Mary, Mother of Jesus".","title":"Christian Bale filmography"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Dilip Kumar (born Muhammad Yusuf Khan; 11 December 1922) is an Indian film actor, producer and activist.","title":"Dilip Kumar"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Also known as the "Tragedy King", he is credited with bringing realism to film acting since his first film which was released in 1944.","title":"Dilip Kumar"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He is considered one of the greatest and most influential actors of all time.","title":"Dilip Kumar"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He has been described as "the ultimate method actor" (natural actor) by Satyajit Ray.","title":"Dilip Kumar"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Kumar is one of the biggest Indian movie stars, and a pioneer of method acting, predating Hollywood method actors such as Marlon Brando.","title":"Dilip Kumar"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Kumar debuted as an actor in the film "Jwar Bhata" (1944), produced by Bombay Talkies.","title":"Dilip Kumar"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" His career has spanned over six decades and over 65 films.","title":"Dilip Kumar"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" Kumar is known for roles in films such as the romantic "Andaz" (1949), the heartwarming "Babul" (1950), the impassioned "Deedar" (1951), the swashbuckling "Aan" (1952), the dramatic "Devdas" (1955), the comical "Azaad" (1955), "Naya Daur" (1957), "Yahudi" (1958), "Madhumati" (1958), "Kohinoor" (1960), the epic historical "Mughal-e-Azam" (1960), the social "Gunga Jamuna" (1961) and "Ram Aur Shyam" (1967).","title":"Dilip Kumar"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Aaron Michael Sidwell (born 12 September 1988) is an English actor and singer .","title":"Aaron Sidwell"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is best known for playing villain Steven Beale in the British soap opera EastEnders, originating the role of Michael Dork in Loserville in the West End and fronting his own pop group, The Boston Plan.","title":"Aaron Sidwell"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He was also the first British actor to play Johnny in Green Day's American Idiot musical.","title":"Aaron Sidwell"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Sidwell is a method actor, known for using Stanislavski technique","title":"Aaron Sidwell"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Hugo Johnstone-Burt (born 1987/1988) is a Scottish-born Australian actor.","title":"Hugo Johnstone-Burt"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He grew up in Sydney and decided to become an actor after attending his first drama class.","title":"Hugo Johnstone-Burt"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Johnstone-Burt graduated from the National Institute of Dramatic Art in 2009.","title":"Hugo Johnstone-Burt"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He appeared in small roles in Australian dramas "Rake", "Sea Patrol" and "", before he was cast as Fish Lamb in "Cloudstreet".","title":"Hugo Johnstone-Burt"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The role earned him two ASTRA Award nominations.","title":"Hugo Johnstone-Burt"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Johnstone-Burt went on to star in "Carelesss Love" and he took on the role of Constable Hugh Collins in ABC1's "Miss Fisher's Murder Mysteries".","title":"Hugo Johnstone-Burt"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" In 2012, Johnstone-Burt appeared in "Tricky Business" and filmed a guest role in "Home and Away".","title":"Hugo Johnstone-Burt"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" He has also appeared in the musical drama film "Goddess" (2013) and the disaster film "San Andreas" (2015).","title":"Hugo Johnstone-Burt"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Daniel Day-Lewis
